  "about": "The simulated league with the teaching normal-normal posterior of app 1.5 (prior mean 0) along the prior SD, .01 to 1. The read-out gives, at the chosen prior SD, the average squared distance from the posterior means to the true values in this draw and over many draws (closed form) beside the estimates', and the pairs with one direction above .90 and above .99; the panels add the pairs against the true order, the units that end farther and where the curves are lowest; the comparison table sets a too-narrow prior (.05) and a too-wide one (.45) beside the estimates; 1.5's lead, units figure and order figure show the league at the chosen prior SD. A new app (a new angle on v1 L-04 view 2): every expected value comes from the base-R oracle (oracle-summaries, oracle-simulate, oracle-v3 for expectedSquaredDistance and pairCertainty) or from v1's frozen registry; settings (prior SD, seed) from the registry's settings keys; the lead and caption are literals of v1 contract rows 9.4 and 6.5 in their v3 wording. Numbers with no oracle row (this draw's distance at .02, .45 and the steps between, the closed form at .05 and .45, pair certainty off prior SD .15, the closed-form minimum searched in steps of .001) are checked by the general rules only (data-num read back). Part 1 review: the distance and certainty values at the chosen prior SD are said once, in the read-out (their panels keep the flat prior's counts only), so the panel hooks sure-90 and sure-99 went; the comparison lead adds that the counts are the posterior's own probabilities.",
